WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:13.832
Device groups let you target a meaningful set of machines
together, such as a pilot site, a product model or a test fleet.
Create a group with a name your team will recognize, instead of
selecting every device for each release.

2
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:25.483
Open Manage and add the devices that belong in this group.
Review membership before deploying, because membership
determines which devices can take part when they check the
deployment.

3
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:35.459
Choose Deploy this version from the component library. Starting
with a published version helps you select the exact release you
already prepared and reviewed.

4
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:49.515
Select the group as the target and review the version and
recipients. This flow creates a one-time deployment. It does not
establish an ongoing rule that automatically brings future group
members onto this release.

5
00:00:50.240 --> 00:01:03.040
Create the deployment and approve the request. Devices still
need to connect, check their eligibility and run the
installation. Approval authorizes the deployment; it does not
mean all targets have finished.

6
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:19.461
Open Deployments to follow each device’s result. Check successes
and failures there rather than relying on the deployment-created
message. If a device fails, inspect the available failure
details before retrying or sending a corrected version.

